WEBVTT

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.160
He did that all by himself?

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:14.820
Incredible.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.240
We were way too late.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:17.120
I'm sorry.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.950
Let's go, too! Get into position!

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:22.710
Doesn't something look wrong?

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:23.790
Subaru?

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.960
H-Huh?

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.880
You're accelerating too much.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.630
Wh-When I'm nervous, I—

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.090
Brakes! Hit the brakes!

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:30.880
U-Uh...

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.470
Why?!

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.350
You're all here again?

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.350
I could say the same to you, Horned Cape!

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.520
What a pathetic five-point star.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.860
You think you can outdo me with that?

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.780
We were looking for that first!

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.120
So what?

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.620
This has nothing to do with you.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.910
I need the fragments of my engine!

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.580
Give it back!

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.620
This belongs to me.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:10.340
It isn't something people as
clumsy as you can handle!

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.510
Where did he...

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:15.470
He's gone.

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:17.260
Yeah...

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:34.570
After-School Pleiades

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:40.740
Sobbingly, I went on my journey

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:45.200
Wishing I could at least fly through the sky

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:51.590
And yet the stars gently shone on me in the nights after our quarrels

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:57.130
I wonder if you were also watching them

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:02.390
I don't know... I want to know... I want to feel it...

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:09.440
Nothingness simply means there are infinite possibilities

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.230
The excitement I got after realizing that

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:16.320
was like surfing the waves of space and time

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:21.410
How strange that I'm not afraid anymore

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:24.120
Let's embrace our imperfections and go on

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:27.000
We'll open the promised door

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:32.170
and gain dazzling smiles!

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:54.020
Five Cinderellas

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.280
I'm hungry...

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.280
Do not

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.280
take home!!!

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:03.620
Cosplay Research Club

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:03.620
Please knock!

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:03.620
No opening when we're changing!

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.710
I hate that guy!

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:14.790
I'm sorry.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.630
It's not just your fault, Subaru.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.760
We'll need to improve our
meteor shower forecast again.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:23.220
It seems like he can do anything,
even though he's all alone.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:28.140
Hey, President, what are we
supposed to be capable of?

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:31.350
Just flying in the sky,
creating poor magic circles?

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:37.690
The reason I chose you to help me was
because of your innate potential.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:44.740
Each of you lies in a gray area,
in which countless potentials overlap,

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:46.120
but none has taken shape.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:49.000
You are neither children nor adults.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.960
As of yet, you are nothing, nor are you
trying to become something.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.330
You are paradoxical beings
who are nearing adulthood

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.880
while holding on to your youthful spirits.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:00.050
I don't really understand, but...

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:01.630
That doesn't really make me happy.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:05.890
You can talk about potential,
but I'm just one person.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:09.520
Yes, we only have one life to live.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:14.350
However, what if all possibilities
capable of occurring existed,

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:17.770
and we are just unable to see them?

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:19.150
Huh?

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:22.450
Even if there's only a
one-in-a-quadrillion chance,

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:24.410
then it happens at least once
every quadrillion times.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:30.330
We possess the technology to secure
one of the outcomes we desire,

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.920
out of all the universe's overlapping possibilities.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:39.000
You all possess such overlapping potentials,
and I secured that outcome,

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.670
in exchange for a vast amount of energy.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.670
So, if I were to answer Hikaru's question,

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:47.550
then you all possess the potential
to be capable of anything.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:52.810
Although, I was supposed to choose
the single best perceivable person,

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:56.560
so five of you appearing was
a great miscalculation—

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:59.440
Well, if that's what an alien says...

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:00.820
We're useless.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:06.700
You may make it sound good, but you're
telling us we're useless nobodies.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.950
Just as many potentials exist, there are
many ways of interpreting them.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.120
So that is one possible answer, as well.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.540
Hmph! What a rude alien!

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:15.960
You're the one who said it!

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.460
I'm kind of worn out...

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.420
Hey, can we go home now?

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.390
I'm home.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.640
Oh, welcome home, Subaru.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.730
What's this, Dad?

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.690
Oh, it's an engine.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:38.650
An engine?

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:40.900
Yeah. I'm building a prototype.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:44.190
This? It has a weird shape.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.150
Does it?

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.110
Hmm...

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:51.330
If you look at the parts separately,
I guess they might look oddly shaped.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:55.500
But everyone thought their
hardest to come up with

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.750
the shape of each and every part.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:01.750
No matter what shape it has,
it's like that for a reason.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:06.380
And once those manufactured
parts are properly assembled,

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:09.010
they produce unbelievable power.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:15.180
But all of these are defective, aren't they?

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:17.310
Are you sure you should've brought them home?

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.270
Non-standard products are a part
of the manufacturing business.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.270
I just couldn't throw them away.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.200
Subaru?

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.080
But...

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:37.040
But no matter how many defective
parts you put together,

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.000
they won't be able to do anything.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:56.600
Hey, Subaru! Did you forget your duty?

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:57.480
Oh...

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.600
I did. I'm sorry.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.600
Cleaning This Week

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.600
Hallway

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.600
Off

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.600
Lab

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.600
Stairway

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.600
2F
bathroom

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.600
Classroom

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:20.540
Why do you always look so down?

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.880
Um, is this... Ah!

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.630
That's my...

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:29.630
It's good.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:34.890
You can have that strawberry milk. As thanks.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:35.760
As thanks?

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:41.140
I was able to become friends again with
the girl I told you about, thanks to you.

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:43.980
What did I do?

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:46.570
You listened to me.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:47.610
That's all?

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:48.150
Yeah.

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:53.160
Still, that helped me feel better.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:58.160
Hmm... Then why are you
making a face like that again?

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:07.670
Because someone called me clumsy again.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.920
That was mean. Another friend?

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:13.720
That man isn't a friend!

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:17.390
But he wasn't wrong.

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:24.020
I'm sure that, of all my potential
selves, I'm the biggest nobody.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.860
Nobody?

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.230
That must be it.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:29.650
That's why I was chosen.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.490
When I can't choose anything...

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:36.740
You must be a greedy person, then.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:37.990
Huh?

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:41.160
You hate to just compromise on things.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:42.910
I just can't make decisions.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:45.420
Oh... I'm jealous.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:47.130
Minato-kun?

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.210
You're free to decide and to hesitate.

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:52.380
You can do as you wish.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.590
I'm not hesitating because I want to!

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:55.800
For example?

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:59.930
Um, maybe I shouldn't be with everyone

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:03.060
if I'm just going to slow them down...

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:08.650
In your eyes, is being with them good or bad?

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:10.780
It's not bad!

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:12.190
Then you want to be with them?

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:13.440
I do!

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.200
You aren't hesitating now.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:16.740
Huh?

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:19.700
Are you sure you aren't actually
just a little frightened?

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:23.330
But are you the only one who's scared?

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:27.080
I need to go.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:27.830
Huh?

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:29.880
I'm sure everyone's waiting for me.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.420
You think so?

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.090
I don't know, but...

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.340
Then you should go.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.350
Can I come visit again?

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:46.350
I still haven't heard anything about you.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:49.360
There are so many things I want to ask you.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:50.650
Who knows...

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:54.360
But if the stars guide you here, then...

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.360
Cosplay Research Club

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:01.580
Stop.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:02.580
Huh?

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.540
Where have you been?

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:07.330
Oh?

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:09.880
We're conducting an experiment for
a new meteor shower forecast.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:10.840
Listen, I—

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:11.460
Stay there.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:12.290
Huh?

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:15.300
The reception just increased.
Raise your right hand.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:16.220
Okay...

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.300
Stand on your left toes.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:18.880
Huh?

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.640
Left hand to forty-five degrees.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:22.970
What can you tell from this?

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:23.970
I have it.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:24.890
Over the sea?

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:26.230
That's awfully far.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.770
We could probably still go
swimming that far south.

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:31.980
The range of the fragments' appearance
is growing wider and wider.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:34.190
Do you think he'll show up again?

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:37.360
Well, he probably will.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.620
I can do this much.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:50.170
If you only try things you can
do already, it's not practice.

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:50.920
Huh?

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:56.050
Thanks...

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:58.260
This is how you practice.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:10:59.300
There!

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:01.180
Now right yourself!

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.640
Easy for you to say!

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.390
Itsuki-chan...

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:09.850
Since we're here, let's have fun practicing.

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.060
Y-Yeah.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:12.940
<i>They aren't like Aoi-chan's!</i>

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:14.900
Come on, Subaru-chan.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:16.940
But the shaft...

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:18.900
You can let go of it.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:21.570
The drive shaft is a part of your body.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:22.910
O-Okay.

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:28.160
Wow, we're so high!

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:31.170
But this is as far as we can go.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:37.340
You know, when I was younger,
I thought everyone could fly.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.840
I hated the fact that I was
the only one who couldn't.

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:44.510
So I enjoy this very much now.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:55.480
Let's go!

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:03.070
We are right on time.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:04.320
Good job, me.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:05.660
That's it, Subaru.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:07.830
D-Don't talk to me right now!

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.580
We should have done it this
way from the start, huh?

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:13.330
Don't let your guard down. Look.

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:22.050
You're working hard,
ladies of the five-pointed star.

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:25.840
Hey! Get your feet off that!

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:30.220
Using the same pattern won't work!

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:34.190
Huh?

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.980
You impudent little...

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:43.530
Huh? The fragment...

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:44.490
Where'd it go?

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:45.070
It disappeared?

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:47.950
Wh-What's going on?

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:02.460
I thought I told you all not to interfere.

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:05.340
Y-You're the one who didn't hold on to it!

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:06.390
Oh...

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:08.350
What is it?

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:09.850
Oh, my.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.180
What a shame!

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:15.850
Now you've lost the engine
fragment you finally found.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:18.060
Since we're in the southern seas,

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.730
we might as well vent our
anger with a little swim.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:26.280
Yeah. I bet that'd feel good.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:28.490
But we don't have anywhere to change.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.830
No one can see us here.

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:32.370
Hey, why don't you join us?

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:36.120
Shameless... Do as you please!

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:39.670
What should I do? I didn't bring a swimsuit.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:41.050
We're just pretending.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.170
Oh, that's it?

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:44.010
There's no need for us to actually—

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.510
It appears there is.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:46.720
Look.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.510
It's in the ocean? We can't—

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:51.850
We certainly can!

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:54.560
We can easily go ten thousand
meters on a single breath!

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:55.520
You're taking this easy.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:14:00.610
Do you think all the laws of physics apply
to you when you're transformed?!

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:02.730
Now, let's go!

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:14.500
<i>Incredible! We're in swimsuits!</i>

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:16.160
<i>I don't feel short on breath at all.</i>

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:19.670
Listen, be very careful not to waste your air!

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:21.670
<i>Same to you.</i>

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.220
<i>It's so dark.</i>

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:37.980
<i>There.</i>

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:47.150
<i>Carefully... Don't scare it.</i>

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:49.740
<i>Wow, it's really dark.</i>

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:52.370
<i>I'm starting to feel a bit cold.</i>

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:01.710
<i>Was Aoi-chan's hand always this cold?</i>

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:04.960
<i>Was Subaru's hand always this big?</i>

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:13.470
<i>Wow...</i>

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:15.970
<i>It's like we're in space!</i>

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:25.480
<i>Huh?</i>

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:27.440
<i>The shape of the magic circle...</i>

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:29.240
<i>Something's different.</i>

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:44.460
<i>Quiet. If you frighten the fragment,
this will all be for nothing.</i>

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.630
<i>Damn it, this is frustrating.</i>

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:14.110
Is everyone all right?

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:14.700
Somehow.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.330
Where did that guy go?

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:20.700
A waterspout?

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:21.960
It's worse than that!

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:25.960
How far up does this go?

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:29.630
Probably to the stratosphere.
Even clouds can't go higher than that.

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:30.800
The stratosphere?

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:33.180
Ten thousand meters up.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:36.430
Itsuki?

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:37.510
Itsuki-chan?

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.440
This is the limit...

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:00.790
That punk!

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.620
I can't believe he can fly higher than Itsuki!

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:06.630
No, I need to feel the wind more...

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:08.130
Itsuki-chan!

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:09.960
Subaru-chan?

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:11.960
H-How's this?

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:20.890
<i>I can see the wind.</i>

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:24.810
I've got it.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:34.030
Incredible. At this rate...

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:36.700
Grab on!

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.160
Wait, how?

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:40.410
I don't know!

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:42.660
We've linked?

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:43.410
Amazing.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.500
So this is the air in the stratosphere?

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.920
Itsuki, you're having too much fun!

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.460
I'm sorry, I was just so happy.

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:53.420
Look, over there!

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:55.420
We found that punk!

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:04.810
Idiots! I told you not to frighten it.

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:14.780
Leave it to me.

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:17.860
Aoi!

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.830
Almost there...

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:32.130
Everyone, the rest is up to you!

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:41.720
Fly into my chest!

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:42.600
Catch!

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:50.190
Aoi-chan!

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:51.150
Subaru!

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:58.150
Uh-oh.

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.550
I'm hungry...

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:18.630
I can't even move.

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:20.050
Me, neither.

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:22.180
Wow...

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.640
There are so many stars...

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.850
Where are we? We're floating!

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:30.140
The Earth's a ball!

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:32.440
It's daytime, and we can see the stars?

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:35.070
We're actually swimming through space...

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:35.820
This isn't over!

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:38.570
You're still here?

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:41.570
Hand over the fragment,
you failed five-pointed stars!

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:43.570
No!

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.160
You again?

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:51.370
Stop, Subaru! He's dangerous!

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:52.670
Huh? My shaft...

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.040
I told you not to interfere.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:59.170
You have neither a reason nor
the resolve to use them!

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:00.590
You're wrong!

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:03.510
I don't know what reason or
resolve you're talking about,

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:06.260
and I may be useless,
but the others are different!

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:10.430
When I couldn't fly well,
they stayed late to help me.

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:12.270
They're all very kind!

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:14.270
They're not failures!

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:16.520
They only did it to make things convenient for them.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:17.820
It wasn't for your sake.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:20.360
No, they're really nice.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:24.280
They're doing their best to help me,
the alien, and each other.

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:27.200
I want to be with them!

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:29.240
I want to be like them!

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:37.540
Do as you like, then!

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:38.380
Subaru?

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:38.800
You did it.

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:40.550
Oh, sorry.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:42.920
Why, you...

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:47.050
Subaru, are you all right?

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:48.140
You did it, Subaru!

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:49.060
Subaru!

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:52.560
Hey, do you hear something?

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:02.150
What's this?

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:03.490
Shooting stars!

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:04.070
These?

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:18.040
It's like we're listening to the sound of space.

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:22.300
Right now, we're in free fall,

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:27.430
being drawn toward the horizon by Earth's
gravity, at 28,000 kilometers per hour.

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:30.640
You're both on Earth and in space.

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:33.810
Either that or in an area that's neither.

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:38.440
It's like a dream, being able to
see the stars from up here...

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:42.820
The less you all are in your own reality,

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:45.700
the more I'm able to turn that
potential into power for you.

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:51.660
And right now, that's allowing you to
physically feel both Earth and space.

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:53.950
This is our power, too?

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:57.790
You see, when I looked up

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:56.670
There are plenty of things that possess

00:21:56.670 --> 00:22:00.460
neither choice nor potential
from the moment they're born.

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:03.880
everyone was smiling at me

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:05.220
Yet I'm very fortunate to have met you all.

00:22:04.630 --> 00:22:13.270
both embarrassed and happy as the starry sky turned sideways

00:22:06.340 --> 00:22:07.340
Cinderella.

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:08.800
What is it?

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:13.520
We're five Cinderellas,
gathered by one glass slipper!

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:14.310
What do you mean?

00:22:14.060 --> 00:22:22.860
Ever since then, whenever my daily life seemed hopeless

00:22:14.310 --> 00:22:15.680
Wh-What?

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:19.480
I mean, we couldn't help but be drawn together...

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:19.980
...my daily life...

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:20.900
What?

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:23.400
Nothing. It just sounds a lot like you.

00:22:22.860 --> 00:22:32.370
I'd go into myself just for a little bit and ask

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:25.860
Aoi-chan, you really love those things, don't you?

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:26.650
What things?

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:27.900
Cute things!

00:22:27.900 --> 00:22:30.370
Huh? I was being serious!

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:33.290
I'm so happy!

00:22:32.620 --> 00:22:33.790
"Can I fly?"

00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:37.330
I'm really happy we can be together, Aoi-chan!

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:38.580
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:41.170
Jeez... I think you're getting
the wrong idea, Subaru.

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:43.840
We can go there whenever we want to

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:42.210
Huh?

00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:45.460
We aren't any different from you.

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:53.850
The wind sows stars in the far distance only light leaps to

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:46.760
We're the same.

00:22:46.760 --> 00:22:51.180
So I'm happy, too!

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:55.560
I've never felt this good before!

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:58.560
"We have to catch them!"

00:22:58.690 --> 00:23:02.900
In the very moment I reached out my hand,

00:22:59.980 --> 00:23:02.190
People aren't like manufactured parts.

00:23:02.650 --> 00:23:06.190
They don't have to settle for
taking only one shape.

00:23:03.110 --> 00:23:08.860
the scenery around us glittered

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:10.950
You haven't even taken any
shape yet, have you, Subaru?

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:13.160
sometime after school

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:14.740
So there's nothing to be sad about.

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:19.960
To Be Continued

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:31.590
You see, there's a reason you get born

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:36.970
Nobody knows what it is

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:46.690
But people still keep searching for a spell to prove their existence

00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:55.660
Days with too much freedom might be too much to handle for some

00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:53.030
...freedom...

00:23:55.660 --> 00:24:05.420
So they keep looking for the very thing to do

00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:07.300
"It'll be fine!"

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:11.510
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:24:11.510 --> 00:24:17.140
If you can't wait, let's go right away

00:24:17.140 --> 00:24:26.820
Each star sticker you stick on will speed you up

00:24:26.820 --> 00:24:31.440
"I want to embrace you!"

00:24:31.440 --> 00:24:35.950
Of course you'll make it

00:24:35.950 --> 00:24:41.290
because the promise between us

00:24:41.540 --> 00:24:46.000
is for all eternity after school

00:24:51.050 --> 00:24:55.300
Space has all kinds of sounds! I'm so moved!

00:24:55.300 --> 00:24:56.760
It's livelier than I expected.

00:24:56.760 --> 00:24:58.890
Just like us, right?

00:24:59.220 --> 00:25:01.270
Next episode: Dream of Sol.

00:24:59.390 --> 00:25:04.980
Next Episode
Dream of Sol

00:24:59.390 --> 00:25:04.980
Next Episode
Dream of Sol

00:25:01.270 --> 00:25:04.310
But that doesn't mean
it isn't a lonely place.
